# Stripe keys live in the ENCRYPTED VAULT, not here: paste them in
# admin → System → Secrets as STRIPE_API_KEY and STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET
# (test keys from https://dashboard.stripe.com/test/apikeys; the webhook secret
# comes from `stripe listen` in dev, or the endpoint config in production).
# Vault writes apply on the next call — no restart. Prefer plain env? Uncomment
# below and point the billing account's secret refs at env instead.
# STRIPE_API_KEY=
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# The vault's master key — encrypts those secrets at rest (the scaffolder
# generated one into .env; rotate with: openssl rand -base64 32)
PATTERN_VAULT_KEY=

# The app's public origin (e.g. https://app.example.com) — checkout redirects
# and emailed links (invites, sign-in) are built on it. Unset in dev = localhost.
# PATTERN_PUBLIC_URL=

# A failed run emails this address (needs a "default" email account)
# PATTERN_ALERTS_TO=
